# Product Test Matrix – Smart Wi-Fi Video Doorbell

## Overview

This portfolio artifact demonstrates how a structured test matrix can be used to plan, document, and organise product testing for a hypothetical Smart Wi-Fi Video Doorbell.

The test matrix includes test IDs, test objectives, priority levels, preconditions, test procedures, expected results, test status, and defect references.

## Test Areas

- Power and startup behaviour
- Power interruption and recovery
- Wi-Fi connectivity and reconnection
- Video streaming
- Continuous operation
- Thermal observations
- Physical inspection
- Connector inspection
- PCB visual inspection
- Power supply and voltage regulator checks
- Notification and event functionality
- Regression testing

## Test Documentation

Each test case is structured to support traceability and consistent test documentation.

The matrix provides fields for:

- Test ID
- Test area
- Test objective
- Priority
- Preconditions and setup
- Test procedure
- Expected result
- Test status
- Defect ID
- Notes

## Testing Approach

The proposed testing approach involves:

1. Reviewing the product requirements and specifications.
2. Identifying the functionality and potential failure points.
3. Defining test conditions and expected results.
4. Performing tests under controlled and safe conditions.
5. Recording actual observations and evidence.
6. Reporting defects where test results do not meet acceptance criteria.
7. Retesting after corrective actions and documenting outcomes.

## Portfolio Disclaimer

This is an illustrative test-planning exercise developed for portfolio and learning purposes. The test cases are proposed scenarios and have not been executed on a physical Smart Wi-Fi Video Doorbell.

The matrix demonstrates structured test planning, documentation, and a systematic approach to product quality assessment.
